    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2002-p6.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Taking \\(n = 1,\\) the inequality becomes \\(m \\le m + 1,\\) which holds for every positive integer \\(m.\\)\n\nSo every positive integer \\(m\\) works, and there are infinitely many.\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Consider what happens when \\(n = 1\\)",
        "For \\(n = 1,\\) the inequality reduces to \\(m \\le m + 1\\)"
